WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.240
Hi, and welcome to
Reframing Problems with AI.

2
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.440
I'm Tacey Baskett, and I'm
your instructor for the course.

3
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.480
I teach computer literacy and Office
software applications at De Anza.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.980
I took this class on because I have been
very proactive in implementing AI in my

5
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.360
courses for years and am passionate
about helping my students learn to use

6
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.440
AI to work smarter, not harder.

7
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.640
Here is what the next 10 weeks are about.

8
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:36.660
You are going to pick one real problem
from your own work or life and understand

9
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.260
it properly.

10
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.540
Who it affects and how, what is already
being done about it, and what you are

11
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.420
assuming or still need to learn.

12
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.600
Going deep is the point.

13
00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.760
In this new world of AI, it has become
very important for you to be able to

14
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.880
clearly explain what you're trying to
solve so that AI can actually help you.

15
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:02.000
You will use AI a lot in this course,
and you will find out where it helps and

16
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.480
where the thinking has to be yours.

17
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.020
I want you to meet three other people
who did a lot of work on the design and

18
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.060
building of this course and who
are working with me to support you.

19
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.780
You'll see them in office hours and one-on-ones, so let's make sure you know who

20
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:18.280
they are.

21
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.030
Hi, I'm Leslie Maxwell, and I'm really
excited to welcome you.

22
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.080
You're going to meet my two other
colleagues here in a minute, and each of

23
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.750
us is going to tell you a little bit more
about what's to come.

24
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.360
So for me, this course is going to ask you
to slow down and really think about a

25
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.810
problem, which might feel a little
uncomfortable.

26
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.190
We tend to want to solve problems quickly
and then move on.

27
00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:43.660
But as many of us are probably finding out
as we work with AI, AI will work

28
00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.370
on whatever you put in front of it.

29
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:50.060
So if you give it the wrong thing or a
half-baked thing, what you get back is

30
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.450
usually not very helpful.

31
00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.360
So one of the real human values in this
age of AI is being able to direct AI

32
00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.770
toward what you actually want.

33
00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.310
And that means really being able to
clearly frame your problem.

34
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.550
So that's what this course is all about.

35
00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:06.930
Thanks.

36
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.810
Hi, I'm Melisa Villafuerte.

37
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.200
Another crazy thing about the introduction
of AI into our lives is how much more

38
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.810
important human conversations have become.

39
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.620
This course will ask you to go and talk to
other people about the problem you're

40
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.440
working on. Getting to know their
perspectives will help you better

41
00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.190
understand the problem that you're trying
to solve and how to go about it.

42
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.150
Hello, everyone. I'm Jeremy.

43
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.050
I helped build the AI Dojo.

44
00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.790
That's going to be the workspace that you
use across every single sprint.

45
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.930
So this isn't a chatbot that you use for
answers.

46
00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.190
You bring it something that you've already
written, your problem, your assumptions,

47
00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.130
your lists, and it reads that information
and pushes back.

48
00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.290
It asks you what you have not checked.

49
00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.930
It points to what is missing.

50
00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.420
So that's why Leslie said, be clear first.

51
00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.590
The AI has nothing to work with until you
give it that context.

52
00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:05.220
You set it up in Sprint 0, and if it ever
starts to behave strangely, just let

53
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.130
us know because that'll help us fix it for
everyone.

54
00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:08.770
Thank you.

55
00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.730
One thing we want to say plainly, this is
the first time this course has run.

56
00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.700
As you know, AI changes and improves
practically week to week, and there was no

57
00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.350
course like this to copy from.

58
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.220
We built it carefully and we are going to
adjust it as we go, based on what we see

59
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.860
from you. You are the first group through
it, and what you tell us changes the

60
00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:30.430
course.

61
00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:35.790
If a page is confusing, if an activity
takes three times longer than we said,

62
00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.370
if the AI does something strange, tell us
early.

63
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.080
The best way to connect with us is office
hours, a one-on-one check-in, or

64
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:50.120
Canvas Chat. We really, truly want to hear
from you, so please take advantage of

65
00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:55.060
these opportunities. You can find all of
the information about how to connect on

66
00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.910
the Get Live Help page in Sprint 0 of the
Canvas course.

67
00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.970
Start with Sprint 0. It is short.

68
00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.050
It sets up your Dojo and walks you through
how the course runs.

69
00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.110
Sprint 1 follows right after that.

70
00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.310
We are glad you're here. See you in office
hours.

